ComfyUI dynamic model reread fix
================================

Based on upstream ComfyUI commit:

    52b2dcd76c8f8281fc1041127f1c743be5e74bab
    Test fix for model reloading issue.

Problem
-------

ComfyUI's execution cache and its dynamic model-weight residency are separate
layers. A loader or LoRA node can correctly appear in `execution_cached` while
the AIMDO dynamic loader still has to make the model weights resident again.

`cast_to_gathered()` was unconditionally calling
`read_tensor_file_slice_into()`. That is the direct file-backed transfer path
intended for `--fast-disk`. With the normal configuration, every dynamic VBAR
fault could therefore reread weight slices from the safetensors backing file
instead of falling through to the normal RAM-backed tensor-copy path.

This was especially visible when changing LoRAs. A new patch signature makes
dynamic weight pages dirty, and the unconditional direct-read path then
restreamed large portions of the base model while rebuilding those pages. Node
caching did not prevent this because the cached object was the ModelPatcher,
not the residency of every weight page.

The observed behavior was intermittent because Linux's page cache could make
later reads cheap. The first sample after a cold or stale residency state was
very slow; after it warmed the file pages and pinned buffers, the same workflow
became fast again. Restarting or switching to one batch prompt changed that
working-set state, which made either action appear to fix the problem.

Fix
---

Use the direct file-slice path only when the user explicitly enables
`--fast-disk`. Otherwise, fall through to the existing tensor-storage path,
which marks the mmap as dirty and copies from the RAM-backed tensor. This lets
the normal pinned-memory and RAM residency mechanisms do their jobs without
requiring `--high-ram`.

Apply from a ComfyUI checkout with:

    git apply /path/to/comfyui_dynamic_model_reread_fix.patch

The running ComfyUI process must be restarted after applying the patch because
`comfy.model_management` is imported at process startup.

diff --git a/comfy/model_management.py b/comfy/model_management.py
index 222005b6..7afcd966 100644
--- a/comfy/model_management.py
+++ b/comfy/model_management.py
@@ -1451,7 +1451,7 @@ def cast_to_gathered(tensors, r, non_blocking=False, stream=None, r2=None):
             dest2_view = dest2_views.pop(0) if dest2_views is not None else None
             if tensor is None:
                 continue
-            if comfy.memory_management.read_tensor_file_slice_into(tensor, dest_view, stream=stream, destination2=dest2_view):
+            if args.fast_disk and comfy.memory_management.read_tensor_file_slice_into(tensor, dest_view, stream=stream, destination2=dest2_view):
                 continue
             storage = tensor._qdata.untyped_storage() if isinstance(tensor, comfy.quant_ops.QuantizedTensor) else tensor.untyped_storage()
             mark_mmap_dirty(storage)
